# There is no mutable top-level constant: a `mut` one would need storage, and
# storage is what substituting a literal avoids. The parser has no such form,
# so it is refused where a declaration would start.

mut COUNT = 1;

fn main() { let x = COUNT; }
--- errors ---
error: expected DocComment, `fn`, `import`, `let`, `pub`, `struct`, or `variant`, found `mut`
 --> ./tests/cases/constants/err_mut.aipl:5:1
  |
5 | mut COUNT = 1;
  | ^^^
